Linux's readings of the ThinkPad T14 this repository is tested on, under that
machine's Ubuntu, read as root on the T14 by `toyos-t14linux/capture.sh` at
commit 44eb3c2e (pull request #601) before 06:50 UTC on 2026-09-29, when
../tcg/ booted the kernel and initramfs the same run copied off the T14. The
script ran only where /proc/version named 6.8.0-142-generic, both packages
were 6.8.0-142.142 and the config's sha256 was config-sha256.txt's, and it read
CPUID and the MSRs through the running kernel's /dev/cpu/*/cpuid and
/dev/cpu/*/msr, so an MSR holds what that kernel left in it.

  vulnerabilities.txt   the run's `grep .` over the vulnerabilities directory,
                        committed as ../t14.txt
  cpuid.txt             CPU 0's leaves, one per line:
                        leaf subleaf eax ebx ecx edx
  msr.txt               one per line: msr cpu value; 0x122 and 0x10F are absent
                        because ARCH_CAPABILITIES bit 7 and CPUID.(7,0):EDX
                        bits 11 and 13 do not enumerate them
  config-hardening.txt  `grep -n` of the config for the options the script
                        names, so an option it did not name is absent, not unset
  kernel-log.txt        this boot's kernel lines from the journal that match, in
                        any case, mitigat, vulnerab, not affected, spectre,
                        microcode, x86/bugs or tsx, and no other
